    <!-- ContentDialog -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Title1">ContentDialog</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Sub1">Modal dialogs for confirmations, inline review flows, and async validation without requiring XamlRoot.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.CC1">Shows a classic modal dialog over the current window. Enter triggers the default button and Escape closes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.CT1">Popup ContentDialog</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.CC2">This example keeps the dialog inside a host region to preview embedded review flows.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.CT2">In-Place ContentDialog</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.CC3">Primary button deferrals can run async work before the dialog is allowed to close.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.CT3">Deferred Validation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.CC4">Declaring an in-place ContentDialog directly in markup.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.CC5">Dialog commands live in the ViewModel; popup creation is isolated behind a dialog service.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Demo1">Theme Preset Preview</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Demo2">The inline dialog below stays inside this card instead of covering the whole window, so you can review changes inline without losing surrounding context.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Demo3">Preset: Studio Contrast</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Demo4">Highlights focused elements with stronger borders, denser surfaces, and a slightly larger review region for modal content.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Demo5">This dialog is shown with ContentDialogPlacement.InPlace.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Demo6">It uses the surrounding card as the host surface, which makes it useful for review and configuration flows embedded in a page.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ContentDialog.Ui1">Show Dialog</x:String>
