    <!-- DragDrop -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.Title1">Drag &amp; Drop</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.Sub1">Demonstrates DragEnter, DragOver, DragLeave, and Drop events, plus the Windows Shell enhancements: a caller-supplied drag image on the source, a Shell drop description on the target, and dragging files out to other applications via DoShellDragDrop.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CC1">Drag items from the source list and drop them into the target area.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CT1">Basic Drag &amp; Drop</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CC2">Drag an item over the zones below to see visual feedback on DragEnter and DragLeave.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CT2">DragEnter / DragLeave Feedback</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CC3">Drag the item below. A caller-supplied image follows the cursor instead of an automatic element clone, using DragDrop.DoDragDrop(source, data, effects, dragImage, offset).</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CT3">Custom Drag Image (drag source)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CC4">Drag one or more files from Windows Explorer onto the area below. Windows renders its own drag image (IDropTargetHelper), and the DragOver handler sets a Shell drop description via e.SetDropDescription(...).</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CT4">Windows Shell Drop (external files)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CC5">Drag the item below onto a Windows Explorer window or the desktop. Unlike the in-app drag, DragDrop.DoShellDragDrop runs a real OLE drag so the file is copied out to another application, with the Windows system drag image.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CT5">Drag Out to Explorer (cross-process)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CC6">Shows DragEnter, DragOver, DragLeave, and Drop events as they fire.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CT6">Event Log</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CC7">Declarative markup for the drag and drop demo above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.CC8">The ViewModel owns state while an attached behavior adapts native drag events.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.Hint1">Drag Source</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.Hint2">Drag me over the zones</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.Hint3">Drag me — custom image</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.DragDrop.Hint4">Drag me to Explorer (creates a .txt)</x:String>

    <!-- EditControl -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Title1">EditControl</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Sub1">A code editor control with syntax highlighting, line numbers, code folding, keyboard navigation, and full undo/redo.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.CC1">Full keyboard navigation, selection, clipboard, undo/redo, and auto-indent.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.CT1">Code Editor with C# Syntax Highlighting</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.CC2">Toggle editor features, then run document commands and load sample code.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.CT2">Architecture</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.CC3">Editing gestures the control recognizes out of the box.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.CC4">How the editor is built under the hood.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.CC5">Declarative markup that configures the editor and its options.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.CC6">The ViewModel owns editor state and commands; a behavior adapts undo, redo, selection, and caret metadata.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body1">{Shortcut.Copy} / {Shortcut.Cut} / {Shortcut.Paste} - Copy / Cut / Paste</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body2">{Shortcut.Undo} / {Shortcut.Redo} - Undo / Redo</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body3">{Shortcut.SelectAll} - Select All</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body4">Home - Smart Home (first non-whitespace / line start)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body5">{Shortcut.WordModifier}+Left/Right - Word Navigation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body6">{Shortcut.DocumentBoundary} - Document Start / End</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body7">Shift+Arrows - Extend Selection</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body8">Tab / Shift+Tab - Indent / Unindent</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body9">Enter - New line with auto-indent</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body10">Double-click - Select word / Triple-click - Select line</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body11">Document Layer: Rope-based buffer (O(log n) insert/delete), DocumentLineTree, UndoStack</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body12">View Layer: Direct DrawingContext rendering with span-based syntax highlighting</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body13">Syntax: ISyntaxHighlighter interface, RegexSyntaxHighlighter with multi-line span support</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.EditControl.Body14">Features: Code folding, bracket matching, find/replace, minimap</x:String>

    <!-- ElementEffects -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.Title1">Element Effects</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.Sub1">Modern element-level visual effects — OuterGlow, InnerShadow, Emboss, ColorMatrix and EffectGroup — each applied to a single element and composable into effect groups.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CC1">Renders a glow around the outer edges of an element. Replaces the deprecated OuterGlowBitmapEffect.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CT1">OuterGlowEffect</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CC2">Renders a shadow inside the element bounds, similar to CSS box-shadow: inset.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CT2">InnerShadowEffect</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CC3">Creates a raised or sunken appearance by simulating light hitting the surface. Replaces the deprecated EmbossBitmapEffect.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CT3">EmbossEffect</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CC4">Applies 5x4 color matrix transformations with preset factories for grayscale, sepia, brightness, contrast, saturation, hue rotation and invert.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CT4">ColorMatrixEffect</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CC5">Composes multiple effects into a single group. Effects are applied sequentially, with each output feeding the next.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CT5">EffectGroup</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CC6">Declarative markup applying element effects through the Effect property.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ElementEffects.CC7">Effect parameters and commands are bound to the ViewModel; visual effect objects remain declarative in XAML.</x:String>

    <!-- Expander -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Title1">Expander</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Sub1">A control with a clickable header that expands and collapses to reveal or hide a section of content, keeping secondary details tucked away until they are needed.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CC1">Click the header to expand or collapse the content region.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CT1">Basic expander</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CC2">An expander can host any content, from checkboxes and dropdowns to full input forms.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CT2">Complex content</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CC3">Expanders can be nested to build collapsible, tree-like sections.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CT3">Nested expanders</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CC4">Drive the expander from code — expand, collapse or toggle it with the buttons.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CC5">Declarative markup for the expanders shown above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.CC6">Wiring the buttons to the expander and handling its expand and collapse events from code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Demo1">Click to expand</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Demo2">This content is revealed when the expander is expanded. You can put any content here including text, images, and other controls.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Demo3">Initially expanded</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Demo4">This expander starts in the expanded state. Click the header to collapse it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Demo5">Controlled Expander</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Demo6">This expander can be controlled using the buttons above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Ui1">Enable notifications</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Ui2">Auto-save documents</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Ui3">Show line numbers</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Ui4">User Profile</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Expander.Ui5">Save Changes</x:String>

    <!-- FlexPanel -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Title1">FlexPanel</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Sub1">A full CSS flexbox container: direction, wrapping, the six justify distributions, cross-axis alignment, and the grow/shrink/basis algorithm from the specification. It is a normal panel — usable from XAML with no CSS in sight — and it is also what display: flex maps onto.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC1">The main axis follows Direction; the reverse variants mirror the placement without touching the Children order.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CT1">Direction</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC2">All six CSS distributions, each with the same three items in the same 100%-wide stage.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CT2">JustifyContent — main-axis distribution</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC3">AlignItems sets the default for the line; AlignSelf overrides it for one item. Stretch is the default and spans the line.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CT3">AlignItems and AlignSelf — the cross axis</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC4">Basis is the item's size before flexing. Free space is handed out in proportion to Grow; a deficit is taken away in proportion to Shrink × Basis, and any item that hits a min or max freezes and its share is redistributed — the resolve-flexible-lengths loop from the specification.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CT4">Grow, Shrink, and Basis</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC5">With Wrap enabled, items break onto new lines and AlignContent distributes those lines along the cross axis.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CT5">Wrap and AlignContent</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC6">Order changes where an item is laid out without touching the Children collection, so focus order, hit testing, and data binding all keep following the declaration order.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CT6">Order</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC7">The whole flex property family maps onto FlexPanel. Nothing below sets a single panel property in markup — the sheet does all of it, including the flex shorthand on the items.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CT7">Driving it from CSS</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC8">The classic flexbox job: a title that takes the slack, actions pinned to the right, everything vertically centred.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CT8">A practical app bar</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC9">Panel properties, attached item properties, and the CSS equivalent.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.CC10">The same panel built imperatively.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Cap1">Use Basis, not Width, for anything that should flex: an explicit Width is a hard constraint the arrange pass always enforces, so a Width-bearing item keeps its size no matter how much free space Grow hands it. Writing flex: 1 in CSS maps to Basis = 0 and does the right thing automatically.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Cap2">Items sharing an Order value keep their declaration order — the sort is stable, as CSS requires.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Cap3">flex-direction, flex-wrap, justify-content, align-items, align-content, gap/row-gap/column-gap, flex (and flex-grow/-shrink/-basis), align-self, and order all map across. On a panel that is not a FlexPanel, the container properties are offered to that panel's own TryApplyCssPropertyCore override — which is how StackPanel turns flex-direction into its Orientation.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage1">Row (default)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage2">SpaceBetween — first and last hug the edges</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage3">SpaceAround — half-size gaps at the ends</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage4">SpaceEvenly — every gap identical</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage5">Stretch (default)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage6">Center, with one item overriding via AlignSelf</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage7">One item grows into all the free space</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage8">Weighted split — free space shared 1 : 3</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage9">Shrink — the two items ask for more than the line holds</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage10">A frozen minimum — the left item cannot go below MinWidth, so the right one absorbs the whole deficit</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage11">Wrap with a row and column gap</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage12">WrapReverse — the line order is mirrored</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage13">flex: 1 — absorbs everything left over</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Stage14">Grow 1 with Basis 0 — the title strip takes all the slack</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.FlexPanel.Tile1">Grow 1 — takes the rest</x:String>

    <!-- Flowchart -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.Title1">Flowchart</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.Sub1">Render directed flowcharts that automatically rank nodes into layers and draw shapes, arrows, and edge labels — authored concisely as mermaid text.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.CC1">A flowchart with decision nodes, branch labels, and a hierarchical (top-to-bottom) layout.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.CT1">Decision Flow</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.CC2">Rectangle, rounded, stadium, circle, rhombus, hexagon, cylinder and more — with solid, dotted, and thick edges in a left-to-right layout.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.CT2">Node Shapes &amp; Edge Styles</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.CC3">Edit the mermaid flowchart source on the left and see the diagram update on the right.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.CC4">Author the flowchart declaratively as mermaid text.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Flowchart.CC5">Render a flowchart from code with MermaidDiagram or FlowchartDiagram.</x:String>

    <!-- Frame -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Title1">Frame</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Sub1">A container that hosts page content and navigates between pages, keeping a back and forward history along the way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CC1">A frame can host and navigate between pages.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CT1">Basic Frame</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CC2">Frame supports back and forward navigation.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CT2">Navigation Controls</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CC3">Common frame configuration options.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CT3">Frame Properties</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CC4">Frame is useful for various navigation scenarios.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CC5">Declarative markup for the frame and its navigation buttons.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.CC6">Navigation state and commands live in the independent ViewModel.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Use1">• Wizard-style interfaces</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Use2">• Multi-step forms</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Use3">• Browser-like navigation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Use4">• Embedded page content</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Use5">• Help system navigation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Ui1">Back</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Ui2">Forward</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Ui3">Show navigation UI</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Ui4">Enable journal (history)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Ui5">Sandboxed navigation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Frame.Ui6">Cache size:</x:String>

    <!-- GanttChart -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.Title1">GanttChart</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.Sub1">A chart control that displays tasks on a timeline with support for dependencies, milestones, and progress tracking.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.CC1">A simple Gantt chart with several tasks spanning different date ranges.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.CT1">Basic Gantt Chart</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.CC2">Gantt chart with dependency arrows between tasks and milestone markers.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.CT2">Dependencies &amp; Milestones</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.CC3">Gantt chart showing partial task completion with progress indicators.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.CT3">Progress Tracking</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.CC4">Declarative markup for the Gantt charts above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GanttChart.CC5">Tasks, dependencies, milestones, and progress are ViewModel collections bound by XAML.</x:String>

    <!-- GaugeChart -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.Title1">GaugeChart</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.Sub1">Displays a value on a radial gauge with colored ranges, tick marks, and a needle indicator.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.CC1">A gauge chart with a simple value, minimum, and maximum.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.CT1">Basic Gauge</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.CC2">A gauge with green, yellow, and red range segments.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.CT2">Colored Ranges</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.CC3">A row of three small gauges showing CPU, Memory, and Disk usage.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.CT3">Multiple Gauges</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.CC4">Declarative markup for the gauges above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GaugeChart.CC5">Gauge configuration and ranges are declared directly in XAML.</x:String>

    <!-- GeographicHeatmap -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.Title1">GeographicHeatmap</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.Sub1">A control that renders a geographic heatmap visualization with Gaussian-blurred intensity fields and configurable gradients.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.CC1">A GeographicHeatmap with scattered heat points around a metropolitan area.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.CT1">Radius &amp; Intensity</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.CC2">Multiple heatmaps demonstrating different Radius and Intensity values.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.CT2">Color Gradients</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.CC3">Heatmaps with different color gradient options: default, warm, and cool.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.CC4">Declarative markup for the heatmaps above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GeographicHeatmap.CC5">Heat points and gradients come from the ViewModel; XAML declares every heatmap variant.</x:String>

    <!-- GettingStarted -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Eyebrow1">JALIUM.UI / START</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Title1">Getting Started</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Sub1">Learn how to build declarative applications with Jalium.UI and a conventional ViewModel boundary.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CC1">Add the UI package to your application project.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CT1">Installation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CC2">A window can be composed in C# when a declarative view is not required.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CT2">Create your first window</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CC3">Declare the visual tree in markup and bind it to a dedicated ViewModel.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CT3">Use JALXAML</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CC4">Use panels to describe layout intent.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CT4">Layout controls</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CC5">Expose observable properties and commands from the ViewModel.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CT5">Data binding</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CC6">Styles can also be written as real CSS. Property keywords are 100% native CSS, and anything CSS has no keyword for reaches the control's dependency properties by its kebab-case name.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.CT6">Styling with CSS</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Panel1">Arranges children in a horizontal or vertical line.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Panel2">Arranges children in rows and columns.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Panel3">Positions children at explicit coordinates.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Panel4">Docks children to the edges of a container.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Panel5">A full CSS flexbox container: grow, shrink, wrap, and the six justify distributions.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Panel6">Hover me — the rule is .demo:hover in a Css.StyleSheet on the parent.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GettingStarted.Panel7">Styled by an inline Css.Style declaration block.</x:String>

    <!-- Grid -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.Title1">Grid</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.Sub1">A flexible layout panel that arranges its children into rows and columns, with fixed, auto and star sizing plus row and column spanning.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.CC1">A 3x3 grid with colored cells labelled by their row and column index.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.CT1">Basic Grid Layout</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.CC2">Key capabilities of the Grid control: mixed sizing, row spanning and column spanning.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.CT2">Grid Features</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.CC3">Declarative markup for an application-style grid layout.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.CC4">Building the same grid layout dynamically in code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Grid.Cap1">This section now uses real RowDefinitions, ColumnDefinitions, RowSpan, and ColumnSpan.</x:String>

    <!-- GroupBox -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Title1">GroupBox</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Sub1">A container that frames a set of related controls under a titled header, giving forms and settings panels clear visual structure.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.CC1">Two GroupBoxes on one row, each framing its own set of fields.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.CC2">What the GroupBox container gives you.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.CC3">Declarative markup for the grouped forms above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.CC4">Building a settings GroupBox and its fields in code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Body1">• Visual grouping of related controls</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Body2">• Customizable header text</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Body3">• Header can contain any content</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Body4">• Styled border around content</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Demo1">Personal Information</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Demo2">Receive updates</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Demo3">Enable dark mode</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.GroupBox.Demo4">Show advanced options</x:String>

    <!-- Heatmap -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.Title1">Heatmap</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.Sub1">Displays a 2D matrix of values as a color-coded grid with optional labels and a color scale bar.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.CC1">A 10x10 heatmap with the default BlueToRed color scale.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.CT1">Color Scales</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.CC2">The same data rendered with the Viridis and Grayscale color scales.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.CT2">Cell Values</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.CC3">A heatmap with ShowCellValues enabled, displaying the numeric value inside each cell.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.CC4">Declarative markup for a heatmap with axis labels and cell values.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Heatmap.CC5">The ViewModel owns matrices and labels; XAML owns heatmap rendering configuration.</x:String>

    <!-- HexEditor -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.Title1">HexEditor</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.Sub1">A hex editor control that displays and edits binary data in hexadecimal format with offset, hex, and ASCII columns.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.CC1">Display and edit binary data with offset, hex, and ASCII columns.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.CT1">Basic Hex Editor</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.CC2">Toggle columns and adjust bytes per row using the controls below.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.CT2">Configuration Options</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.CC3">A read-only hex viewer for inspecting binary data without modification.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.CC4">Declarative markup for the hex editors above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HexEditor.CC5">Binary data and editor configuration are bound from the ViewModel.</x:String>

    <!-- HyperlinkButton -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Title1">HyperlinkButton</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Sub1">A button styled as a hyperlink that navigates to a URI or runs a click handler, with automatic hover, pressed and underline states.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.CC1">Standalone links navigate to a URI; links can also flow inline inside a sentence.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.CC2">Key capabilities provided by the control out of the box.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.CC3">Declarative markup for the links above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.CC4">Creating and wiring links in code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Body1">• Navigate to external URLs</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Body2">• Hyperlink styling (underline, color)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Body3">• Hover and pressed states</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Body4">• Opens in default browser</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Cap1">In paragraph context:</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Ui1">Visit Microsoft</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Ui2">Open GitHub</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.HyperlinkButton.Ui3">Learn More</x:String>

    <!-- IconElement -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.Eyebrow1">ICONOGRAPHY</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.Title1">IconElement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.Sub1">A family of scalable vector icons — SymbolIcon, FontIcon, and PathIcon — drawing 600+ glyphs from Segoe Fluent Icons for buttons, toolbars, and app bars.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CC1">Use the Symbol enum to display common icons from Segoe Fluent Icons.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CT1">SymbolIcon</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CC2">Use a glyph from any font and control its size and color through bindings.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CT2">FontIcon</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CC3">AppBarButton.Icon accepts an IconElement rather than a raw string.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CT3">AppBarButton with SymbolIcon</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CC4">Every Symbol enum value is supplied by the ViewModel and grouped alphabetically.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CT4">Complete Symbol Enum Gallery</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CC5">Declarative markup for SymbolIcon, FontIcon, and AppBarButton icons.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.IconElement.CC6">A dedicated ViewModel supplies icon data to reusable XAML templates.</x:String>

    <!-- Image -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Title1">Image</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Sub1">Displays raster and vector images with four stretch modes, plus corner rounding, borders and clipping supplied through its ControlTemplate.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CC1">Image loaded from a remote URL with Stretch.Uniform.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CT1">Remote image</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CC2">Compare the four stretch modes side-by-side using the same image.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CT2">Stretch modes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CC3">A vector image rendered as true vector graphics — sharp at any resolution, with no quality loss when scaled.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CT3">SVG image</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CC4">Compare the four stretch modes with an SVG vector image.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CT4">SVG stretch modes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CC5">The Image control supports CornerRadius, a border and a background brush through its ControlTemplate.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CT5">Styled images</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CC6">The key properties the Image control exposes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CC7">Declarative markup for loading and styling images.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.CC8">Creating BitmapImage and SvgImage sources and Image controls in code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Body1">Source - The ImageSource to display (BitmapImage or SvgImage)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Body2">Stretch - How the image fills its area (None, Fill, Uniform, UniformToFill)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Body3">StretchDirection - Limits scaling direction (UpOnly, DownOnly, Both)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Body4">Background - Background brush behind the image (via ControlTemplate)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Body5">CornerRadius - Rounded corners with clipping (via ControlTemplate)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Body6">BorderBrush / BorderThickness - Border around the image (via ControlTemplate)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Cap1">Original size, no scaling</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Cap2">Fills container, may distort</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Cap3">Fits inside, preserves ratio</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Cap4">Fills container, clips overflow</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Cap5">Rounded</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Cap6">Circle</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Cap7">Bordered</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Val1">Stretch.None</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Val2">Stretch.Fill</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Val3">Stretch.Uniform</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Image.Val4">Stretch.UniformToFill</x:String>

    <!-- InfoBar -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.Title1">InfoBar</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.Sub1">A notification bar for surfacing important, non-blocking status messages inline, without interrupting the user.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.CC1">Each severity paints its own accent, icon and tint; the last bar can be dismissed with its close button.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.CC2">What the InfoBar control supports out of the box.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.CC3">Declarative markup for the InfoBars above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.CC4">Creating, showing and dismissing notifications from code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.Body1">• Four severity levels (Info, Success, Warning, Error)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.Body2">• Title and message content</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.Body3">• Optional close button</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.Body4">• Action button support</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InfoBar.Body5">• Custom content area</x:String>

    <!-- InkCanvas -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.Title1">InkCanvas</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.Sub1">A drawing surface that captures freehand ink strokes from mouse, pen or touch, with configurable stroke color, width, brush type and eraser modes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC1">Draw with your mouse, switch between ink and erase modes, or clear the canvas.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CT1">Basic Drawing</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC2">Pick a color to draw with.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CT2">Stroke Color</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC3">Adjust the width of the stroke.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CT3">Stroke Width</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC4">Toggle highlighter mode for semi-transparent strokes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CT4">Highlighter Mode</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC5">Select the brush type used for new strokes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CT5">Brush Type</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC6">Select the taper style for new strokes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CT6">Taper Mode</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC7">Shows the number of strokes currently on the canvas.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CT7">Stroke Information</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC8">Declarative markup for the InkCanvas demo above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.InkCanvas.CC9">The ViewModel exposes drawing state and commands; an attached behavior adapts the InkCanvas instance API.</x:String>

    <!-- JsonTreeViewer -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.Title1">JsonTreeViewer</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.Sub1">A control that displays JSON data in an interactive tree view with search, expand/collapse, and path copying.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.CC1">Display structured JSON data with color-coded types and expandable nodes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.CT1">Basic JSON tree</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.CC2">Type in the search box to highlight matching keys and values in the tree.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.CT2">Search &amp; filter</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.CC3">Enter JSON text on the left and see the tree view update on the right.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.CC4">Declarative markup for the JSON tree viewers above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.CC5">JSON content and live search state are exposed by the ViewModel.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.Ui1">Search keys or values...</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.JsonTreeViewer.Ui2">JSON Input:</x:String>

    <!-- Label -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.Title1">Label</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.Sub1">A control that displays text and can be associated with a target element, so clicking the label or pressing its access key focuses the partner control and improves form accessibility.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.CC1">Each caption is a Label paired with its input; click a label to focus the field beside it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.CC2">What the Label control brings to a form.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.CC3">Declarative markup binding each label to its target through an access key.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.CC4">Creating labels and wiring their Target in code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.Body1">• Associates label with target control</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.Body2">• Click label to focus target</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.Body3">• Access key support (Alt+Key)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Label.Body4">• Improves form accessibility</x:String>

    <!-- LineChart -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.Title1">LineChart</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.Sub1">Displays data as connected line segments with optional smoothing, area fill, and data point markers.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.CC1">A single data series rendered as a line chart with data point markers.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.CT1">Basic Line Chart</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.CC2">Overlay multiple data series on the same chart with a legend.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.CT2">Multiple Series</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.CC3">Catmull-Rom spline smoothing with a filled area beneath the line.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.CT3">Smoothed Line &amp; Area</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.CC4">Declarative markup for a line chart with a single series.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LineChart.CC5">Series are declared in XAML and bind to data collections owned by the ViewModel.</x:String>

    <!-- LiquidGlass -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.Title1">Liquid Glass</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.Sub1">Apple-style liquid glass effect with SDF-based refraction, chromatic aberration, edge highlights, and inner shadow. Set LiquidGlass=True on any Border control.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC1">Background refraction with edge highlights and inner shadow. BlurRadius=8, RefractionAmount=60.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CT1">Default Liquid Glass</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC2">Add rainbow-edge dispersion effect. ChromaticAberration controls the amount of color separation.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CT2">Chromatic Aberration</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC3">Liquid glass adapts the SDF shape to different corner radii.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CT3">Corner Radius Variants</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC4">Set Background on the Border to apply a colored tint over the glass effect.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CT4">Tinted Liquid Glass</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC5">Adjust blur radius, refraction amount, and chromatic aberration in real-time.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CT5">Interactive Parameters</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC6">Adjacent liquid glass panels fuse together with smooth metaball-like blending via SDF smooth minimum (smin). Panels must be siblings in the same parent Panel.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CT6">Liquid Glass Fusion</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC7">Set Shape=SuperEllipse for iOS-style squircle borders. SuperEllipseN controls the exponent (2=circle, 4=iOS, higher=more rectangular).</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CT7">SuperEllipse Shape</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC8">Without Liquid Glass (solid fill)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC9">Set LiquidGlass properties on Border:</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC10">Declarative markup for applying the liquid glass effect to a Border.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.LiquidGlass.CC11">Wiring the interactive sliders and setting glass properties in code-behind.</x:String>

    <!-- ListBox -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.Title1">ListBox</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.Sub1">A scrollable container that presents a collection of items and lets the user select one or many.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.CC1">Click an item to select it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.CC2">ListBox supports several selection modes, keyboard navigation and data binding.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.CC3">Declarative markup for creating and populating a ListBox.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.CC4">Populating items and handling selection in code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.Body1">• Single selection mode (default)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.Body2">• Multiple selection mode</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.Body3">• Extended selection mode ({Shortcut.PrimaryModifier}/Shift)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.Body4">• Keyboard navigation (Up/Down/Home/End)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.Body5">• ItemsSource binding</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListBox.Body6">• ItemTemplate support</x:String>

    <!-- ListView -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Title1">ListView</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Sub1">A scrollable collection control that presents items as a plain list or as multi-column rows, with single, multiple, or extended selection.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CC1">A vertical list of selectable items.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CT1">Basic ListView</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CC2">Switch to a GridView to lay items out across labelled columns.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CT2">ListView with columns</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CC3">Single, multiple, and extended selection each behave differently on click and drag.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CT3">Selection modes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CC4">Add and remove items, and watch the selection readout update.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CC5">Patterns where a list-based layout fits naturally.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CC6">Declarative markup for the lists above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.CC7">Populating, editing, and observing selection in an independent ViewModel.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Cap1">Single Selection</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Cap2">Multiple Selection</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Cap3">Extended Selection</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Chip1">File explorers</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Chip2">Email lists</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Chip3">Contact lists</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Chip4">Task managers</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Chip5">Log viewers</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ListView.Ui1">Enter item text</x:String>

    <!-- MapView -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.Title1">MapView</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.Sub1">A map control that displays slippy-map tiles with support for markers, polylines, panning, and zooming.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.CC1">A MapView centered on Beijing with default zoom controls and scale bar.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.CT1">Basic Map</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.CC2">A MapView with labeled markers at key locations and a polyline connecting them.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.CT2">Markers &amp; Overlays</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.CC3">Interactive zoom and pan demo. Use the buttons to zoom in/out or click the map to pan.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.CT3">Zoom Controls</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.CC4">Declarative markup for the maps shown above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MapView.CC5">Map data, viewport state, and commands are exposed by the ViewModel.</x:String>

    <!-- Markdown -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Title1">Markdown</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Sub1">Render rich Markdown documents with headings, lists, tables, code fences, and relative links.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CC1">Switch between a few representative Markdown documents and see the rendered output update live.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CT1">Interactive Preview</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CC2">Type Markdown in the input box on the left and see the rendered output update live on the right.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CT2">Custom Styling</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CC3">The control can inherit the surrounding theme or use native styling properties for article-like layouts.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CT3">Mermaid Diagrams</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CC4">Fenced mermaid code blocks render as diagrams (flowcharts, pie charts) instead of source. See the Charts &gt; Flowchart page for the standalone control.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CT4">Markdown Properties</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CC5">Key properties for setting the source, resolving relative links, and shaping the native renderer.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CT5">Selection &amp; Copy</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CC6">Drag to select text (or press {Shortcut.SelectAll}), then copy with {Shortcut.Copy} or the right-click menu. The control copies in three formats — plain text, Markdown source, and rich text (HTML + RTF) — and exposes the text for translation and other integrations.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CC7">Declarative markup for the Markdown controls above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.CC8">Text, samples, copy commands, and live-editor state are supplied by the ViewModel.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Body1">Text - Markdown source string rendered by the control</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Body2">BaseUri - Resolves relative links and images in the generated HTML</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Body3">LinkForeground / CodeBackground / QuoteBorderBrush - Native styling hooks for rich content</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Body4">Background / Foreground / FontFamily / FontSize - Shape the native renderer typography</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Cap1">Markdown Input:</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Cap2">Rendered Output:</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Cmd1">Docs Sample</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Cmd2">Release Notes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Cmd3">Copy as Plain Text</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Cmd4">Copy as Markdown</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Cmd5">Copy as Rich Text</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Markdown.Cmd6">Select All</x:String>

    <!-- MediaElement -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.Title1">MediaElement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.Sub1">A control that plays audio and video media, with transport controls, volume and playback-speed options.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CC1">Load a local file or URL, then control playback with ViewModel commands.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CT1">Video player</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CC2">The same MediaElement plays audio and reports playback progress through a behavior.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CT2">Audio player</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CC3">Adjust shared playback options for both players.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CT3">Playback controls</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CC4">Common video and audio container and codec formats are supported.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CT4">Supported formats</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CC5">Declarative bindings for media source and playback options.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.CC6">Media source, options, and transport commands are owned by the ViewModel.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.Body1">Video: MP4, WebM, AVI, WMV, MOV</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.Body2">Audio: MP3, WAV, AAC, OGG, FLAC</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.Ui1">Video File:</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.Ui2">Enter video file path or URL...</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.Ui3">Audio File:</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MediaElement.Ui4">Enter audio file path or URL...</x:String>

    <!-- Menu -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.Title1">Menu</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.Sub1">A horizontal command bar whose items open drop-down lists of commands, keyboard shortcuts and nested submenus.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.CC1">A standard menu with multiple items.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.CT1">Basic Menu</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.CC2">Menu items can display keyboard shortcuts.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.CT2">Menu with Keyboard Shortcuts</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.CC3">Menu items can contain nested submenus.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.CT3">Nested Submenus</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.CC4">Declarative markup for the menus above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Menu.CC5">Building a menu and wiring item click handlers in code-behind.</x:String>

    <!-- MenuBar -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuBar.Title1">MenuBar</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuBar.Sub1">A horizontal bar that organizes application commands into top-level menus with flyout submenus.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuBar.CC1">A standard menu bar with File, Edit, View, and Help menus, each with keyboard-gesture hints.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuBar.CT1">Basic MenuBar</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuBar.CC2">Click menu items to see which action was triggered.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuBar.CT2">Menu Action Log</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuBar.CC3">Declarative markup for the menu shown above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuBar.CC4">Building the menu and wiring click handlers in code-behind.</x:String>

    <!-- MenuFlyout -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.Title1">MenuFlyout</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.Sub1">A flyout menu that displays a list of commands or options, typically opened from a button click.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.CC1">Click the button to open a context menu with common actions.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.CT1">Basic MenuFlyout</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.CC2">Menu items can display icons alongside their labels for quick identification.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.CT2">MenuFlyout with Icons</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.CC3">Menu items can be toggled on and off to control view options.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.CT3">MenuFlyout with Checkable Items</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.CC4">Declarative menus bind directly to ViewModel commands and state.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MenuFlyout.CC5">The ViewModel exposes ICommand properties and checkable option state.</x:String>

    <!-- MiniMap -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.Title1">MiniMap</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.Sub1">A mini-map control that shows a scaled-down overview of a target element with a draggable viewport rectangle.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.CC1">A ScrollViewer with large content and a MiniMap that tracks the visible area. Click the mini-map to navigate.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.CT1">Basic MiniMap</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.CC2">A MiniMap targeting a MapView to provide a geographic overview with viewport indicator.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.CT2">Map Integration</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.CC3">Multiple MiniMaps showing the None, Outline, and Simplified render modes side by side.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.CT3">Render Modes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.CC4">Declarative markup for wiring a MiniMap to a ScrollViewer or MapView target.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.MiniMap.CC5">The ViewModel supplies content and markers; target relationships and render modes are declarative XAML.</x:String>

    <!-- NavigationDemo -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.Title1">Navigation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.Sub1">WPF-compatible navigation with NavigationService, JournalEntry, and NavigationWindow.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CC1">Provides navigation methods and maintains back / forward history.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CT1">NavigationService</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CC2">Represents entries in navigation history with custom state support.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CT2">JournalEntry</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CC3">A Window with built-in navigation chrome including back / forward buttons.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CT3">NavigationWindow</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CC4">Save and restore page state during navigation. Includes DictionaryContentState and ScrollContentState.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CT4">CustomContentState</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CC5">Declarative markup for a NavigationWindow, navigation buttons, and an embedded Frame.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.NavigationDemo.CC6">Navigating, handling navigation events, and opening a NavigationWindow in code-behind.</x:String>
