    <!-- TextEffectPresenter -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TextEffectPresenter.Title1">TextEffectPresenter</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TextEffectPresenter.Sub1">Per-character animated text surface for lyrics, subtitles, notifications, and playful UI.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TextEffectPresenter.CC1">Each button triggers a call on the presenter — new graphemes enter, existing ones shift or dissipate.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TextEffectPresenter.CT1">Mutation API</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TextEffectPresenter.CC2">Swap the per-cell animation driver. Each button re-enters the text so you see the full enter animation.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TextEffectPresenter.CT2">Built-in Effects</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TextEffectPresenter.CC3">The per-cell animation (TextEffect) runs first on CPU, then the whole surface goes through a GPU pixel-shader pass (UIElement.Effect). Toggle a BlurEffect on top to see the two layers compose.</x:String>
