    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TimePicker.Lbl6">30 minute steps:</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TimePicker.Lbl7">Select time:</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TimePicker.Lbl8">Alarm Time</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TimePicker.Lbl9">Meeting Start Time</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TimePicker.Lbl10">Reminder Time</x:String>

    <!-- TitleBar -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.Title1">TitleBar</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.Sub1">A customizable window title bar with standard minimize, maximize, and close caption buttons you can wire to real window actions.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.CC1">Toggle which caption buttons appear, flip the maximized state, then click the title bar controls to update the status line.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.CT1">Notes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.CC2">How this demo maps onto a real application window.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.CC3">Declarative markup for a TitleBar and its caption buttons.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.CC4">Creating a TitleBar and wiring its caption events in code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.Body1">This area represents window content under a custom title bar.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.Body2">In a real window, these buttons are usually wired to minimize, maximize, and close actions.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.Body3">Use Window.TitleBarStyle = Custom to let the Window host its built-in TitleBar integration.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.TitleBar.Body4">This gallery page keeps all actions local and only updates demo state.</x:String>

    <!-- ToastNotification -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Title1">ToastNotification</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Sub1">A transient overlay that surfaces brief, self-dismissing notifications in a corner of the window without blocking the user.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CC1">Fire a toast at each severity level and watch it appear in the overlay host.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CT1">Basic toast notifications</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CC2">Static examples of how each severity renders inside a toast.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CT2">Toast preview</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CC3">Toasts can include action buttons; trigger one to see the action handler respond.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CT3">Toast with actions</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CC4">Set the host position and duration, toggle the close button and auto-dismiss, then show a custom toast.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CT4">Toast configuration</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CC5">Declarative markup for the toast host and preview items above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.CC6">Toast state and commands live in the ViewModel; the overlay host is adapted by a behavior.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Ui1">Download Complete</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Ui2">Your file has been downloaded.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Ui3">Show Toast with Actions</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Ui4">Show close button</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Ui5">Auto-dismiss (pause on hover)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Ui6">Show Custom Toast</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToastNotification.Ui7">Dismiss All</x:String>

    <!-- ToggleSwitch -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.Title1">ToggleSwitch</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.Sub1">A switch control that flips between on and off states, with an optional header and customizable on/off content.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.CC1">Flip each switch to change its on/off state.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.CC2">What the ToggleSwitch control supports out of the box.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.CC3">Declarative markup for the switches above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.CC4">Handling the Toggled event and creating switches in code-behind.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.Body1">• Binary on/off toggle state</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.Body2">• Customizable on/off content</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.Body3">• Header text support</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.Body4">• Animated state transitions</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToggleSwitch.Body5">• Touch and mouse interaction</x:String>

    <!-- ToolBar -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.Title1">ToolBar</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.Sub1">A container that groups related commands and controls into a single band, using separators to cluster them into logical groups.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CC1">A toolbar with buttons.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CT1">Basic ToolBar</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CC2">Toolbars can contain various types of controls.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CT2">ToolBar with Mixed Controls</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CC3">Multiple toolbars can be organized in a tray.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CT3">ToolBar Tray</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CC4">Click toolbar buttons to see the action.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CC5">Declarative markup for the toolbars above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolBar.CC6">Creating a toolbar and wiring button clicks in code-behind.</x:String>

    <!-- ToolTip -->
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.Title1">ToolTip</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.Sub1">A lightweight popup that reveals contextual help when the pointer hovers over a control, supporting both plain strings and rich, structured content.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CC1">Hover over the buttons to see tooltips.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CT1">Basic ToolTip</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CC2">ToolTips can be added to any control.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CT2">ToolTips on Various Controls</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CC3">ToolTips can contain rich content with multiple elements.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CT3">Rich Content ToolTip</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CC4">ToolTips can be positioned at different locations.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CT4">ToolTip Placement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CC5">Declarative markup for the tooltips above.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.ToolTip.CC6">Setting tooltips and building rich content in code-behind.</x:String>
