    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero7">WPF-grade ergonomics, a GPU-accelerated renderer, one XAML dialect across desktop, mobile and web — with every control proven live in this gallery.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero8">Enter the Gallery</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero9">press [ enter ] to load the gallery</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero10">120+ controls · live · gpu · native-aot</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero11">SPECIMENS</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero12">A few live, hand-set from the collection</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero13">GPU compositing</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero14">Hardware acceleration</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.Overview.Hero15">frosted · refractive glass</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.GridTitle">CSS Grid with native controls</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.GridCaption">Three flexible tracks, automatic placement and spanning. The StackPanel keeps its children and switches layout when display:grid is applied.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.SubgridTitle">Nested controls sharing grid tracks</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.SubgridCaption">The nested StackPanel uses subgrid to share its parent's columns and gaps. Its padding stays inside the shared tracks, and its children retain their native parents.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.FlowTitle">Block and inline flow</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.FlowCaption">Inline controls wrap to the next line. A block starts its own row and fills the available width, while the native control objects stay in place.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.MarginCollapseCaption">Adjacent 20px and 32px vertical margins collapse to a 32px gap.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.FloatTitle">Float placement and clearance</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.ContainerTitle">Respond to container width</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.ContainerCaption">Drag to resize the card. Its content switches between one and two columns at 360px, and the indicator stays at 10% of its content width. The width uses a native XAML binding.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Loc.P.CssLayout.FloatCaption">Inline controls wrap beside the floating card. The final block clears both sides, and flow-root contains the float.</x:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
